WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.677
Causal masking prevents the decoder from cheating during training.

00:00:03.677 --> 00:00:11.107
Suppose the sequence is “natural language processing is useful.” When the model is learning to predict

00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:16.332
processing, it should be allowed to use natural and language, but not is or useful,

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:20.637
because those tokens are in the future relative to the prediction position.

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:25.752
A causal mask blocks attention from each position to later positions.

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:34.757
In an attention matrix, that produces a triangular pattern: tokens can attend backward to earlier context and

00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:36.332
usually to themselves, but not forward.

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:40.692
During actual generation, the future tokens do not exist yet,

00:00:40.692 --> 00:00:44.462
so the same causal structure matches inference naturally.

00:00:44.462 --> 00:00:49.467
Do not confuse causal masking with the padding attention mask we used earlier.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:53.112
Padding masks hide artificial padded positions.

00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:58.812
Causal masks hide future positions to preserve autoregressive generation.

00:00:58.812 --> 00:01:02.480
A model may use both kinds of masking at the same time.
